WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.884
A stranger receives a professional message. Instead of answering what

00:00:04.884 --> 00:00:09.218
it says, he becomes interested in whether software touched its grammar.

00:00:14.175 --> 00:00:18.129
Someone may write in a second language, seek clarity and

00:00:18.129 --> 00:00:22.083
still be treated as if the improvement itself discredits the speaker.

00:00:26.675 --> 00:00:31.068
Before mocking a junior colleague, imagine announcing to your boss or

00:00:31.068 --> 00:00:35.460
an established native speaker that their polished prose makes them a bot.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:46.226
For years academics were instructed, and sometimes charged, to have manuscripts

00:00:46.226 --> 00:00:51.986
professionally edited. The expectation of standardized language did not originate with AI.

00:00:58.217 --> 00:01:02.482
Software assistance does not automatically certify a bad

00:01:02.482 --> 00:01:06.747
argument; nor does an unedited mistake certify originality.

00:01:11.592 --> 00:01:15.709
The essay challenges an etiquette where suspicion is directed

00:01:15.709 --> 00:01:19.826
disproportionately at people without the status to answer back.
